# Wiki codec fixtures are byte-exact test data. Several of them exist precisely
# to test CRLF line endings and a UTF-8 BOM, so Git must not normalize them on
# checkout or commit — normalization would silently rewrite the thing under test
# and the CRLF fixture would pass everywhere by becoming an LF fixture.
test/fixtures/wiki/** -text

# These two fixtures intentionally look invalid to Git's patch checker: one
# carries CRLF bytes and the other carries literal conflict markers. Suppress
# textual diff inspection only for those exact files; the rest of the fixture
# corpus still participates in `git diff --check` normally.
test/fixtures/wiki/adversarial/crlf.md -diff
test/fixtures/wiki/malformed/merge-conflict.md -diff

# The synthesized migration corpus is byte-exact for the same reason: the
# insertion-only property compares prose before and after migration byte for
# byte, and a checkout that rewrote line endings would compare the wrong thing.
# It lives outside test/fixtures/wiki/ so the P2a oracle's "every fixture is
# claimed by an expectation" meta-test keeps meaning exactly what it says.
test/fixtures/wiki-migration/** -text

# Capabilities goldens pin the CLI's exact LF JSON output on every platform.
test/fixtures/capabilities/*.json text eol=lf

# The vendored statechart workflow is pinned byte-for-byte, including its EOF.
skills/mex-statechart/upstream/** -text whitespace=-blank-at-eof
